# =====================================================================
#  tb_controller  --  unit test for controller.sv (phase FSM)
# =====================================================================
#  Parameters    : ROWS=4  FLUSH_CYCLES=6  STORE_LATENCY=8
# 
#  PHASE SEQUENCE AND EXPECTED LENGTHS
#    IDLE     wait for start, latch num_vectors
#    WLOAD    4 cycles   shift the weight matrix into the array
#    FLUSH    6 cycles   drain weight residue from the psum registers
#    COMPUTE  N cycles   one activation vector per clock
#    DRAIN    8 cycles   the last result is still in flight
#    DONE     1 cycle    pulse done, return to IDLE
#    total    N + 19 cycles from the edge that consumes start
# 
#  Phase lengths are measured by COUNTING CLOCKS with each enable high,
#  not by inspecting the state encoding, so a re-encoded FSM still passes.
# 
#  TEST PLAN
#    T1  reset state: IDLE, not busy, not done, all enables low
#    T3  a normal 8-vector job, every phase length checked
#    T2  start hammered throughout a job must change nothing
#    T6  num_vectors=1, the shortest real job
#    T7  num_vectors=0 must not hang
#    T8  back-to-back jobs of different lengths
#    T9  reset mid-job, then the FSM must accept a fresh job
#    T4  phase enables mutually exclusive at all times (continuous)
#    T5  done never overlaps busy (continuous)
# =====================================================================
# 
#   -----------------------------------------------------------------
